    <caption>
      <location value="90"/>
      <location value="320"/>
      <location value="449"/>
      <location value="452"/>
      Appendix Figure S 2.6.4: Results of utilizing image embeddings for possibly improving disease-state prediction. (a) Comparisons of different classifiers under the SampleCV mode using selected metrics (n=3 per group; triangle, mean; center line, median; box limits, upper and lower quartiles; whiskers, up to 1.5 × interquartile range; points, outliers). (b) Comparisons of different input settings under the SampleCV mode using selected metrics. Here spEMO represents the combination: Pseudobulk+Virchow2+Oversample (OS) (n=3 per group; triangle, mean; center line, median; box limits, upper and lower quartiles; whiskers, up to 1.5 × interquartile range; points, outliers). (c) The confusion matrices of all validation sets under the SampleCV mode. (d) The C-index comparison across different input settings for survival prediction (n=5 per group; triangle, mean; center line, median; box limits, upper and lower quartiles; whiskers, up to 1.5 × interquartile range; points, outliers). (e) The training loss curves of survival prediction between two modes with or without image embeddings.
    </caption>
