      <location value="341"/>
      •
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="147"/>
      <location value="339"/>
      <location value="161"/>
      <location value="341"/>
      Disease:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="162"/>
      <location value="339"/>
      <location value="215"/>
      <location value="341"/>
      Colorectal adenocarcinoma (COAD)
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="343"/>
      <location value="190"/>
      <location value="346"/>
      Histopathological Findings:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="346"/>
      <location value="403"/>
      <location value="349"/>
      The provided image represents a histological section of colon tissue associated with colorectal adenocarcinoma. Histopathological analysis focuses on observable cellular and
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="350"/>
      <location value="255"/>
      <location value="352"/>
      structural abnormalities characteristic of malignant processes in the colon.
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="353"/>
      <location value="174"/>
      <location value="355"/>
      Genetic Analysis:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="356"/>
      <location value="252"/>
      <location value="358"/>
      Identified are the top 10 highly variable genes pertinent to the condition:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="359"/>
      <location value="160"/>
      <location value="361"/>
      1.CXCL8
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="160"/>
      <location value="359"/>
      <location value="293"/>
      <location value="361"/>
      : Involved in inflammation, potentially contributing to tumor invasiveness and angiogenesis.
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="363"/>
      <location value="156"/>
      <location value="366"/>
      2.HBB
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="156"/>
      <location value="363"/>
      <location value="317"/>
      <location value="366"/>
      : Known for hemoglobin production, changes here might relate to hypoxia within the tumor microenvironment.
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="146"/>
      <location value="368"/>
      <location value="150"/>
      <location value="370"/>
      …
    </text>
