    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="160"/>
      <location value="382"/>
      <location value="162"/>
      Histopathological Assessment:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="162"/>
      <location value="343"/>
      <location value="164"/>
      •
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="343"/>
      <location value="162"/>
      <location value="371"/>
      <location value="164"/>
      Microscopic Features:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="165"/>
      <location value="404"/>
      <location value="167"/>
      The histology of the provided sample, characterized
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="167"/>
      <location value="396"/>
      <location value="169"/>
<![CDATA[by an H&E-stained whole-slide image, shows]]>    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="170"/>
      <location value="405"/>
      <location value="172"/>
      atypical glandular structures proliferating within the
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="173"/>
      <location value="398"/>
      <location value="174"/>
      colonic mucosa. These glandular units exhibit
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="175"/>
      <location value="393"/>
      <location value="177"/>
      irregular architecture, loss of normal crypt
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="178"/>
      <location value="403"/>
      <location value="180"/>
      organization, and notable cellular atypia, including
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="180"/>
      <location value="403"/>
      <location value="182"/>
      nuclear pleomorphism and hyperchromasia. There
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="183"/>
      <location value="400"/>
      <location value="185"/>
      is evidence of a desmoplastic stromal response,
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="186"/>
      <location value="395"/>
      <location value="187"/>
      indicative of invasive tumor growth. Areas of
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="188"/>
      <location value="396"/>
      <location value="190"/>
      necrosis and hemorrhage may be present, as
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="191"/>
      <location value="398"/>
      <location value="192"/>
      suggested by heterogeneous staining patterns.
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="193"/>
      <location value="343"/>
      <location value="195"/>
      •
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="343"/>
      <location value="193"/>
      <location value="376"/>
      <location value="195"/>
      Tumor Microenvironment:
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="196"/>
      <location value="397"/>
      <location value="198"/>
      The tumor is infiltrated by inflammatory cells,
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="198"/>
      <location value="395"/>
      <location value="200"/>
      including neutrophils and lymphocytes. The
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="201"/>
      <location value="400"/>
      <location value="203"/>
      presence of stromal and immune cells suggests
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="204"/>
      <location value="401"/>
      <location value="205"/>
      ongoing host-tumor interactions. Angiogenesis is
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="206"/>
      <location value="401"/>
      <location value="208"/>
<![CDATA[also likely, given the tumor's cellular density and]]>    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="342"/>
      <location value="209"/>
      <location value="377"/>
      <location value="210"/>
      probable neovascularization.
    </text>
    <text>
      <location value="382"/>
      <location value="162"/>
      <location value="401"/>
      <location value="165"/>
      GPT4-o1
    </text>
